1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,380
Excuse me, I was told to come here for advice about, erm, Management Diploma courses?

2
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:11,500
You've certainly come to the right place. Hi, my name is Monica.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,720
Nice to meet you. My name is Andrew, Andrew Harris.

4
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:20,840
So, Andrew, have you seen our diploma course prospectus yet?

5
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,091
Yes, I've already looked at it.

6
00:00:23,091 --> 00:00:27,592
In fact, I thought the information on course content was really useful,

7
00:00:27,592 --> 00:00:33,969
but I'm afraid I'm a bit confused by all the different ways you can do the course:

8
00:00:33,969 --> 00:00:36,220
full-time intensive, part-time and so on.

9
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:39,142
Well, let's see if I can help.

10
00:00:39,142 --> 00:00:43,316
I think each course type has its advantages and disadvantages,

11
00:00:43,316 --> 00:00:45,620
so it really depends on you

12
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,995
your own study habits, and your financial circumstances, of course.

13
00:00:49,995 --> 00:00:52,500
Are you working at the moment?

14
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:58,463
Yes. I've been working in the administration section of the local hospital for the last three years.

15
00:00:58,463 --> 00:01:04,075
And before that I worked in the office of a computer engineering company for two years.

16
00:01:04,075 --> 00:01:07,582
So, I've got about five years of relevant work experience.

17
00:01:07,582 --> 00:01:11,090
And what I'm hoping to focus on is Personnel Management.

18
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:15,561
I see. And are you planning to leave your current job to study,

19
00:01:15,561 --> 00:01:19,000
or are you thinking about just taking a year off?

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,026
I want to know what my options are, really.

21
00:01:22,026 --> 00:01:25,300
I don't want to quit my job or anything

22
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:29,086
and my employers are keen for me to get some more qualifications

23
00:01:29,086 --> 00:01:32,000
but obviously, it would be better

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,810
if I could do a course without taking too much time away from work.

25
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:40,400
Right, so you don't really want to do the full-time course, then?

26
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,331
No, not really. It's also a question of finances.

27
00:01:43,331 --> 00:01:47,890
You see, my office have agreed to pay the cost of the course itself,

28
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:52,774
but I would have to take unpaid leave if I want to study full-time and,

29
00:01:52,774 --> 00:01:58,310
well, I don't think I could afford to support myself with no salary for a whole year.

30
00:01:58,310 --> 00:02:00,782
OK. Well, you have two other possibilities:

31
00:02:00,782 --> 00:02:05,373
you could either do the part-time course that would be over two years

32
00:02:05,373 --> 00:02:09,820
and you wouldn't have to take any time off work

33
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,084
or you could do what we call a 'modular' course.

34
00:02:12,084 --> 00:02:16,840
You could do that in eighteen months if you wanted, or longer

35
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,500
it's quite flexible and it would be up to you.

36
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:23,500
Mmm. So what does the part-time course involve?

37
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:28,776
For that you would join an evening class and have a lecture twice a week.

38
00:02:28,776 --> 00:02:33,700
Then, you'd have to attend a seminar or discussion workshop one weekend a month.

39
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,380
What kind of coursework would I have to do?

40
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:40,573
Well, it's a mixture. You'd be expected to write an essay each month,

41
00:02:40,573 --> 00:02:43,100
which counts towards your final assessment

42
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,701
You have a case study to do by the end of the course,

43
00:02:46,701 --> 00:02:49,927
which might involve doing a survey or something like that,

44
00:02:49,927 --> 00:02:54,120
and also you need to hand in a short report every four weeks.

45
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:59,008
So, that's quite a lot of work, then, on top of working every day.

46
00:02:59,008 --> 00:03:02,150
It sounds like a lot of studying, and really tiring.

47
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:07,300
Yes, you certainly wouldn't have much free time!

48
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:11,500
What about the 'modular' course? What would I have to do for that?

49
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,735
That's where you get the opportunity to study full-time for short periods.

50
00:03:15,735 --> 00:03:19,040
That way you can cover a lot of coursework

51
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,735
and attend lectures and seminars during the day.

52
00:03:21,735 --> 00:03:26,676
And each module lasts for one term, say, about twelve weeks at a time.

53
00:03:26,676 --> 00:03:29,720
There are obvious advantages in this

54
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:33,382
The main one being that you can study in a much more intensive way,

55
00:03:33,382 --> 00:03:35,500
which suits some people much better.

56
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:40,180
And how many of these 'modules' would I have to do to get the diploma?

57
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:43,580
The current programme is two modules, and

58
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:47,688
then you have to choose a topic to work in more depth, but you can base that on your job,

59
00:03:47,688 --> 00:03:50,860
and so you don't need to be away from the office

60
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,694
and how long it takes is up to you.

61
00:03:53,694 --> 00:03:57,297
The important thing is that you don't have to study and work.

62
00:03:57,297 --> 00:04:00,000
You can focus on one thing at a time.

63
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Yes, I can see that. It certainly sounds attractive!

64
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,180
It would be more expensive, though

65
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:09,000
I mean, I'd have to support myself without pay for each module.

66
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,260
That's true, so that might be a problem for you

67
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:15,860
Look, why don't you talk this over with your employers and...
